@startuml
actor Administrator
participant "Admin UI" as UI
participant "Admin gateway" as Gateway
participant "Core" as Core
participant "GotIt Backend" as Backend
database "product_gotit" as DB
participant "Pixabay or OpenAI" as Provider
Administrator -> UI: Search/filter every user's words
UI -> Gateway: GET words / detail / image / section
Gateway -> Core: Authenticate verified administrator
Gateway -> Backend: Fixed allowlisted read
Backend -> Core: Verify application-scoped administrator
Backend -> DB: Scoped projections and cached image only
Backend --> UI: Metadata, image, paginated histories
Administrator -> UI: Stock replacement or AI prompt + create
UI -> Gateway: regenerate (operationId, expectedRevision, source)
Gateway -> Core: Require content.write and MFA
Gateway -> Backend: Fixed concept regenerate route
Backend -> Core: Independently require permission and MFA
Backend -> DB: Short transaction: receipt + reserved image revision
Backend -> DB: Claim unused revision, keep current image
Backend -> Provider: Reviewed meaning; exclude current photo or use AI prompt
alt Valid provider result and unchanged active meaning
  Backend -> DB: Transaction: validate revision/claim, store asset,
  note right: Advance image pointer and revision; publish audit
  Backend --> UI: Stable success receipt
  UI -> Gateway: Refresh word/concept and image reads
else Provider unavailable or stale meaning
  Backend -> DB: Release claim; retain current image
  Backend --> UI: Unavailable or conflict; preserve retry UUID/payload
end
@enduml
